.TH panicast 1 "2026-08-01" "panicast-V0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
panicast \- Terminal-based media player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B panicast
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
panicast is a powerful terminal-based podcast and radio player with an ncurses interface.
It supports TuneIn radio streaming, RSS podcast subscriptions, YouTube playback, and local media files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B service \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Manage the background service (a USER systemd unit; sudo-free). Subcommands:
\fBinstall\fR (generate/refresh the unit; never starts it), \fBuninstall\fR (stop,
disable and remove the unit), \fBstart\fR, \fBstop\fR, \fBrestart\fR,
\fBenable\fR, \fBdisable\fR (autostart only — never starts/stops the instance),
\fBstatus\fR (service + playback status; the init system is the truth source, a
mismatching pid file is flagged as an anomaly).
Options: \fB--json\fR (machine-readable output on every subcommand; status carries
scope/unitPath/installed/enabled/running/pid/uptimeSeconds/lastExitCode/lastError/
restartCount/platformInit), \fB--user\fR (the default) and \fB--system\fR (accepted
for interface uniformity but refused with exit code 4 — panicast is user-scope by
design).
Bare aliases (\fBpanicast start\fR, \fBpanicast status\fR, ...) dispatch
identically. Exit codes: 0 success / 1 invalid arguments / 2 insufficient
privileges / 3 service operation failed / 4 unsupported scope.
Logs are viewed with native tools (no built-in log command):
\fBtail \-F ~/.local/share/panicast/panicast\-$(date +%Y%m%d).log\fR.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-daemon
Run the headless daemon: the same engine as the TUI with a NullFrontend \(em playback,
queue, subscriptions, downloads and the remote-control servers run without a terminal
(Squeezer / the web remote is the UI). Foreground process; SIGTERM (Ctrl+C) exits
cleanly. Refuses to start when another daemon instance is already running. The systemd
unit runs this mode: \fBpanicast.service\fR (manage via \fBpanicast service
start/stop/restart/status\fR; \fBstart\fR while already running is an idempotent
no-op — use \fBrestart\fR to recycle). A failed mini-LMS bind is fatal here (the
daemon exits non-zero; systemd's restart policy self-heals).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-a \fIURL\fR, \-\-add \fIURL\fR
Add a new subscription from the specified URL.
.TP
.B \-i \fIFILE\fR, \-\-import \fIFILE\fR
Import subscriptions from an OPML file.
.TP
.B \-e \fIFILE\fR, \-\-export \fIFILE\fR
Export subscriptions to an OPML file.
.TP
.B \-t \fITIME\fR, \-\-timer \fITIME\fR
Set a sleep timer. TIME can be in formats: 30m (30 minutes), 2h (2 hours), or 1:30:00 (1 hour 30 minutes).
.TP
.B \-\-purge
Clear all cached data and reset the application.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Pure audio mode (equivalent to --vo=null --vid=no). Disables video output and video track decoding.
.TP
.B \-\-vid <value>
Override mpv video track setting (auto or no). Overrides [mpv] vid in config.ini.
.TP
.B \-\-vo <value>
Override mpv video output driver (e.g., auto, null, gpu, wlshm). Overrides [mpv] vo in config.ini.
.TP
.B \-\-ao <value>
Override mpv audio output driver (e.g., pulse,alsa, pulse, alsa, pipewire, auto). Overrides [mpv] ao in config.ini. Default = pulse,alsa (pulse first, alsa fallback; avoids auto's pipewire-probe stderr on WSLg).
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B j / Down
Move down
.TP
.B k / Up
Move up
.TP
.B g
Go to first item
.TP
.B G
Go to last item
.TP
.B h
Collapse folder / Go back
.TP
.B l / Enter
Expand folder / Play the selected episode. The sibling episodes under the same
parent node (the "peers") become the implicit play list; playback advances through
them according to the current play mode. Marked items: plays the first marked episode.
.SS Playback
.TP
.B Space / p
Play/Pause
.TP
.B + / \-
Volume up/down
.TP
.B [ / ]
Speed down/up
.TP
.B \\
Reset speed to 1.0x
.SS Play Mode & Play Context
There is no separate, persisted play list. The play list is always the peers
(sibling episodes) of the episode currently playing — including all favourite
episodes when playing directly under Favorites root. A single track is loaded
into mpv at a time; on end-of-track the application advances an internal pointer
according to the play mode.
.TP
.B :
Open the command window and type a play mode: the first letter
.BR r ,
.BR s ,
.B c
or the full word
.BR repeat ,
.BR shuffle ,
.BR cycle
(case-insensitive). The mode is global and persisted to
.B [playback] mode
in the config file.
.TP
.B repeat (r)
Single-track loop — the current episode replays (mpv loop-file).
.TP
.B shuffle (s)
Random next episode. Three upcoming random indices are pre-generated so the
INFO preview shows the real upcoming tracks.
.TP
.B cycle (c)
Sequential list loop — advance to the next peer and wrap around at the end.
This is the default.
.PP
The right-hand INFO area shows a 7-line play context while playing:
3 most-recent global history episodes (up arrows), the current episode
(highlighted), and the 3 upcoming episodes (down arrows) per the current mode.
.SS Mode Switching
.TP
.B R
Radio mode
.TP
.B P
Podcast mode
.TP
.B F
Favorites mode
.TP
.B H
History mode
.TP
.B O
Online search mode
.TP
.B Y
Account mode (Google accounts, Y01). Manage multiple Google accounts with independent
YouTube subscriptions and watch history. Each account is a tree node with "播放历史"
and "订阅列表" children. Press
.B a
to log in one account via a QR code (Google OAuth device flow), or
.B A
to log in an additional account.
.B l/Enter
activates the selected account,
.B r
re-syncs its subscriptions and watch history, and
.B d
deletes it. The active account's OAuth token is automatically used by yt-dlp/mpv for
YouTube playback and downloads (login state, bypasses bot verification).
.TP
.B M
Cycle through modes
.SS Y Mode (Google Accounts) [Y01]
.TP
.B a
Log in one Google account: displays a QR code (requires libqrencode; falls back to a text
code otherwise) encoding the Google OAuth device-flow verification URL. Scan it with a phone,
authorize, and the account is added and set active.
.TP
.B A
Log in ANOTHER Google account (add an additional account alongside existing ones).
.TP
.B l , Enter
On an account node: activate it (set as the active account). On "播放历史"/"订阅列表":
expand its children. On a channel: load its videos. On a video: play it.
.TP
.B r
Re-sync the selected account's YouTube subscriptions and watch history.
.TP
.B d
Delete the selected account and all its per-account YouTube data (after confirmation).
.PP
All account data is stored in the single SQLite database
(~/.local/share/panicast/panicast.db); OAuth tokens are encrypted at rest with a
machine-bound key. Existing podcast/radio/favorites/history data stays global and is
unaffected by Y mode.
.SS Other
.TP
.B a
Context action: add feed (Podcast mode), subscribe to podcast (Online mode), or add a local media folder (Favourite mode).
.TP
.B f
Add to favorites
.TP
.B d
Delete item
.TP
.B D
Download the selected episode, or batch-download all marked episodes if any marks are set.
.TP
.B e
Edit the selected node's title and URL.
.TP
.B m
Toggle the mark on the selected node (used for batch play/download/favourite).
.TP
.B v
Enter Visual (multi-mark) mode from the cursor.
.TP
.B V
Clear all marks.
.TP
.B o
Toggle sort order (ascending/descending) of the current list.
.TP
.B r
Refresh the selected node (re-fetch its feed / re-expand). In Account mode, re-sync the
selected account's YouTube subscriptions and watch history; on the Subscriptions or History
container, re-sync only that subtree. In Bilibili mode, re-fetch the followings / history
under the cursor (or re-expand the account node). In TikTok mode, re-fetch the creator's
video list online and replace the local cache.
.TP
.B b
Switch region (Online mode: iTunes storefront region; TikTok mode: TikTok/Douyin region).
.TP
.B N
Jump to the currently-playing node.
.TP
.B S
Toggle scroll mode for long lines in the tree/LOG areas.
.TP
.B U
Toggle icon style (ASCII vs Emoji).
.TP
.B C
Clear the implicit peer playlist while keeping the current track playing (stops auto-advance).
.TP
.B L
Toggle the LYRIC (unified subtitle) bar. Source priority: local SRT > online transcript > ASR.
In Favourite mode, transcribe the selected or v-marked episodes with whisper.cpp to .srt.
.TP
.B :
Open the command window: type a play mode (r/s/c or repeat/shuffle/cycle), an mpv native
hotkey (see MPV HOTKEYS below), or
.B asr
to force real-time ASR on the playing track.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Set the cookies.txt path (context: YouTube / Bilibili / TikTok-Douyin) for yt-dlp and mpv.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Cycle through 22 color themes (Solarized Dark, Gruvbox, Nord, Dracula, Catppuccin Mocha, One Dark, Rose Pine, Monokai Pro, etc.).
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Open the network proxy configuration dialog. Accepts
.BR socks5h:// host:port ,
.BR socks5:// host:port ,
.BR socks4:// host:port ,
.BR http:// host:port ,
or
.BR https:// host:port .
A bare
.B socks://
is normalized to
.BR socks5h:// .
Empty value disables the proxy (direct/transparent proxy). Applies to all curl fetches and yt-dlp invocations; takes effect immediately without restart.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Y
Copy the URL of the object under the cursor (podcast feed, episode, local folder, or online item)
to the system clipboard. Falls back to the playing item's URL when the cursor has none. If the
cursor object has a transcript, its transcript URL is also written to the log (to investigate
episodes that show the 📜 marker but load no lyric). Requires a clipboard helper
(xclip/xsel/wl-copy/pbcopy/clip.exe); otherwise the URL is only logged.
.TP
.B Mouse
Left-click a node in the tree to select and expand/play; mouse wheel to scroll
.TP
.B /
Search
.TP
.B ?
Show help
.TP
.B q
Quit
.SH "MPV HOTKEYS (: COMMAND WINDOW)"
