.SH LAYOUT
The terminal is split into a left panel (feeds tree) and a right panel (INFO + LOG),
plus a 3-row status bar at the bottom. The split ratios are set in
.B [display]
of config.ini:
.B layout_ratio
(left:right, default 0.25 = 25:75) and
.B log_height_ratio
(LOG share of the right panel, default 0.3 = INFO:LOG 70:30).
.PP
.B LOG compression.
.B log_compress_height
(default 23) is the terminal height (including the 3-row status bar) at/above which the
INFO:LOG ratio holds. When the terminal height drops below it, the LOG area is compressed:
LOG loses one row per row of height loss (INFO is preserved \[em] the progress bar and
playback status are prioritized over LOG), and LOG is hidden entirely once it would fit
fewer than 2 rows (INFO then takes the whole right panel). It is configurable so a
different display/resolution can adjust the threshold.
The terminal window size is controlled by the terminal emulator and cannot be locked or
prevented from shrinking by the application \[em] this is a degradation threshold, not a
hard window lock. The ratios are approximate (±1 column/row) due to the character grid.
.SH YOUTUBE (P MODE vs Y MODE)
YouTube support has two independent modes (either or both may be used):
.PP
.B P mode
(PODCAST/ONLINE): subscribe/parse YouTube channels via
.B yt-dlp
+ cookies. Needs
.I youtube_cookie.txt
,
.I yt-dlp
, a JS runtime
.RI ( quickjs-ng ),
and (in GFW) a proxy. No Google login required.
.PP
.B Y mode
(ACCOUNT): scan-code Google OAuth login. Subscription list / search / episode list use the
YouTube Data API v3 (OAuth token, no cookies/yt-dlp needed).
.B Playback still needs cookies
+ yt-dlp + JS runtime (the OAuth token cannot be used for playback — yt-dlp 2026.07 removed OAuth playback).
.PP
Both modes share the same yt-dlp args (cookies + player_client + js_runtime) and the
.I episode_cache
DB table, so fixes to these shared components apply to both.
.SH YOUTUBE CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B [youtube] cookies_file
Netscape cookies.txt path (single source, no browser fallback). Empty/bare
.I youtube_cookie.txt
resolves to
.IR ~/.local/share/panicast/youtube_cookie.txt .
Set via
.B Ctrl+B
Required for playback (bot-check bypass).
.TP
.B [youtube] player_client
Default
.IR tv_downgraded,web
(yt-dlp's official default for cookie-authed requests; least likely to trip "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot").
.TP
.B [youtube] js_runtime
Default
.IR quickjs
(resolve
.I qjs
/
.I qjsng
on PATH, pass
.BI \-\-js\-runtimes " quickjs:<path>"
). Also accepts
.IR deno ,
.IR "quickjs:/path" ,
or empty (yt-dlp default = deno).
.TP
.B [youtube] play_format_video
yt-dlp
.B \-f
format for VIDEO playback. Default
.IR "bestvideo[height<=1080]+bestaudio/best"
(1080p DASH; video+audio separate streams, mpv merges via audio-file; needs ffmpeg). YouTube has no 1080p single file, so 1080p REQUIRES this DASH form.
.TP
.B [youtube] play_format_audio
yt-dlp
.B \-f
format for audio-only playback. Default
.IR bestaudio/best
(highest audio quality).
.TP
.B [youtube] sub_lang
YouTube subtitle language code to load as soft subtitles (Y11). Empty = no subtitles (default,
opt-in). e.g.
.IR en , " zh-Hans" , " ja" .
When set,
.B resolve_youtube_url
also runs
.I "yt-dlp --write-subs --write-auto-sub --sub-langs <lang> --sub-format vtt --skip-download"
to fetch a .vtt, and mpv loads it via
.B sub-file
(per-file option). Soft subtitles are centered by default and respond to
.B F/G
(size),
.B r/R
(position),
.B z/Z
(sync),
.B v
(visibility). Burned-in (hardcoded) subtitles cannot be changed (they are part of the video).
.TP
.B [youtube] sub_auto
.I true
(default): use auto-generated captions when no manual subtitle exists for
.IR sub_lang .
.TP
.B OAuth client (Y mode)
Three methods (priority: runtime file > baked builtin > fallback):
(1) drop
.I client_secret*.json
into
.IR ~/.local/share/panicast/ ;
(2) put
.I secrets/client_secret.json
in the source tree before build (CMake auto-detects and bakes it);
(3) use the built-in fallback client. See
.BR secrets/client_secret.json.example .
.SH BILIBILI (B MODE, Y15)
B mode supports Bilibili video login, browse, search, play and download.
No JS runtime needed (Bilibili has no nsig challenge).
.PP
QR scan = cookie acquisition (like Y mode OAuth scan = token acquisition).
The SESSDATA cookie obtained via QR scan is written to bilibili_cookie.txt and
shared between B mode (following list) and P mode (playback — high resolution requires login).
Video list (WBI-signed arc/search API) does NOT require login; only the following list and
high-res playback do.
.TP
.B a
Login via QR scan (Bilibili passport API → SESSDATA cookie).
.TP
.B A
Login another Bilibili account (QR scan, same as a).
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Set Bilibili cookie file path (context-aware: in B mode → [bilibili] cookies_file).
.TP
.B l / Enter
Expand account (following list via WBI API) / UP master (video list via WBI API) / play video.
.TP
.B /
Search Bilibili (yt-dlp bilisearch).
.TP
.B [bilibili] cookies_file
Netscape cookies.txt path (default <data_dir>/bilibili_cookie.txt).
QR login writes SESSDATA here automatically. Ctrl+B can set a custom path.

.SH "TIKTOK / DOUYIN (T MODE, Y24.11)"
T mode supports TikTok and Douyin (Chinese TikTok) video subscription and playback,
anonymous (no login). Region is shown in the status-bar border (e.g. TIKTOK [US], 抖音 [CN]);
the root node label is static.
.PP
TikTok creator listings work anonymously via yt-dlp (tiktok:user). Douyin has NO user-list
extractor in yt-dlp (no DouyinUserIE), so Douyin supports only single-video playback (option A);
Douyin user URLs are rejected with a message.
.TP
.B T
Enter T mode.
.TP
.B a
Add: @user, a tiktok.com video URL, or a douyin.com video URL.
A TikTok video URL auto-subscribes its @user (the @user is in the URL); expanding lists all
that creator's videos. A Douyin video URL is saved as a playable leaf (Douyin can't list users).
.TP
.B /
Open: @user / #tag / URL. NO anonymous keyword search (search engines don't index
tiktok.com/douyin.com content pages and yt-dlp has no search extractor).
#tag browses the tag via yt-dlp (currently dormant — yt-dlp tiktok:tag is _WORKING=False upstream;
auto-works if re-enabled).
.TP
.B b
Cycle region: US JP GB DE FR KR ID TH VN MY BR MX CN. CN = Douyin (douyin.com); the other 12
are TikTok regions (tiktok.com) with --geo-bypass-country <CC>.
.TP
.B l / Enter
Expand a TikTok creator → its video list (yt-dlp --flat-playlist) / play a video.
.TP
.B d
Delete the item under the cursor.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Import cookie (context-aware: in T mode CN region → [tiktok] douyin_cookies_file; else
[tiktok] cookies_file). Netscape cookies.txt. TikTok works anonymously; Douyin needs a cookie
(fresh, not necessarily logged in) + a China network exit.
.TP
.B [tiktok] region
T-mode region code (default US). b cycles; persisted.
.TP
.B [tiktok] cookies_file
Optional TikTok Netscape cookies.txt (default <data_dir>/tiktok_cookie.txt). Anonymous works without it.
.TP
.B [tiktok] douyin_cookies_file
Douyin Netscape cookies.txt (default <data_dir>/douyin_cookie.txt). Required for Douyin (fresh cookie).

.SH "TRANSCRIPTION (whisper.cpp, Y24.30)"
Offline speech-to-text for episodes without subtitles, via whisper.cpp. Produces an SRT sidecar
(<file>.srt next to the media) that is auto-loaded on replay (probe_sidecar). Real-time
transcription is Y24.30 (not yet).
.PP
Dependencies (user-installed): Arch \(en sudo pacman -S whisper-cpp; Debian \(en sudo apt install
whisper.cpp (or build from https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp). Download a GGML model from
https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp (small.en-q5_1 for capable CPUs, tiny.en for weak).
.TP
.B L (F mode)
Transcribe the local file under the cursor, or the v-marked files. Queues offline jobs;
ffmpeg (to 16kHz mono WAV) + whisper-cli (to SRT) per file, concurrency ≤
.B [transcription] max_concurrent
(default 3, dynamic CPU-load aware via getloadavg). The SRT is saved as <file>.srt and the node
is updated (replay or press r to load).
.TP
.B [transcription] whisper_bin
Path to whisper-cli (default whisper-cli; use an absolute path if built from source).
.TP
.B [transcription] model
Path to the GGML model file (e.g. ggml-small.en-q5_1.bin).
.TP
.B [transcription] max_concurrent
Max concurrent offline jobs (default 3); the dispatcher ramps within [1, max] based on CPU load.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/panicast/
Data directory containing database and cache
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/panicast/panicast.db
SQLite database file. Holds subscriptions, history, favourites, progress, and the
media cache (table
.BR media_cache :
URL \(-> cached/downloaded flags + local file path). On first launch after upgrade
from a version that used
.IR cached_urls.json ,
the cache is migrated into the database in one transaction and the legacy JSON file
is renamed to
.I cached_urls.json.migrated
(only after the DB write commits).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/panicast/downloads/
Downloaded media files
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/panicast/youtube_cookie.txt
Netscape-format YouTube cookies for yt-dlp playback (set via
.B Ctrl+B
or [youtube] cookies_file). Default cookie location.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/panicast/client_secret*.json
Optional runtime Google OAuth client (Y mode). If present, overrides the built-in client.
.TP
.I secrets/client_secret.json
Source-tree OAuth client (optional). If present at CMake configure time, baked as the built-in default. Gitignored.
.TP
.I ~/.config/panicast/config.ini
Configuration file. Sections include
.B [display]
(theme_index: 0-8 color scheme; layout_ratio: left:right panel split, default 0.25 = 25:75; log_height_ratio: LOG share of the right panel, default 0.3 = INFO:LOG 70:30; log_compress_height: terminal-height threshold below which LOG is compressed, default 23, see LAYOUT),
.B [colors]
(customizable node-tree state colors: currently_playing, downloaded, stream_cached, db_cached, parse_failed),
.B [network]
(proxy: socks5h://host:port or http://host:port, empty=direct),
.B [playback]
(mode: repeat|shuffle|cycle — the global play mode), and
.B [statusbar_color]
(status bar color mode). See the file header for the full color-code reference.
